 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A conductor lets heat or electricity pass through it easily. Metals are good conductors of both: copper, aluminium, iron, silver.\nAn insulator does not let heat or electricity pass easily: plastic, wood, rubber, glass, dry cloth, air.\nThermal insulation keeps heat in or out: wooden or plastic handles on pots, a flask with a vacuum, woollen clothes, ceilings under a tin roof, cold boxes for fish.\nElectrical insulation keeps us safe: plastic covering on wires, rubber gloves and boots for electricians, plastic plugs and switches.\nWater with salts in it conducts electricity: never touch switches with wet hands.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "p": "a cooking pot"
  },
  "problem": "Explain why {p} is made of aluminium but has a plastic handle.",
  "steps": [
   "Aluminium is a good conductor of heat: it carries heat from the fire to the food.",
   "Plastic is an insulator: the handle stays cool enough to hold."
  ],
  "answer": "The metal conducts heat to the food; the plastic handle insulates the hand.",
  "checks": []
 },
